  "id": "COMPOUND:781 - DISEASE:2357",
  "verbalization": "Gentamicin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Osteogenesis imperfecta, perinatal lethal through its interaction with osteoglycin. The evidence suggests that Gentamicin affects osteoglycin, which in turn contributes to the development of the condition. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, all of which highlight a direct causal link between Gentamicin and osteoglycin, followed by a downstream effect on the disease. The consistent scoring across the three paths reinforces the reliability of this mechanism. The involvement of osteoglycin as a key mediator underscores a potential therapeutic target, though further research is needed to fully elucidate the precise role of Gentamicin in this process.",
